    "dv": {
      "description": "Antemortem tooth loss (AMTL) treated as a binomial outcome: number of missing teeth of the given tooth class (num_amtl) out of the number of observable sockets (sockets). The model uses the proportion (num_amtl / sockets) with sockets as the binomial denominator (weights).",
      "columns": [
